@page "/docs/components/panel"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Panel
<PageTitle>Panel - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Panel</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="panel" />
        </div>
        <p>A side panel that pushes its siblings aside instead of covering them. There is no backdrop and no focus trap, so the rest of the page stays interactive, which makes it a good fit for item details, inspectors and contextual editors. It sits in normal flow and is bounded by its parent, so place it in the page for a full-height panel or in any container for a contained one. When you need an overlay that blocks the page, use the <a href="docs/components/sheet">Sheet</a>.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(PanelUsageExample)"
                Description="Make the panel a flex sibling of your main content and bind `Open` to any button. Use a row flex parent for `Start` and `End`, or `flex-col` for `Top` and `Bottom`. While closed, the panel is inert, so nothing inside it can be tabbed to or read." />

    <CompositionTree Root="Anatomy"
                     Description="Every part of a panel. The header and footer stay pinned while the content scrolls, and `BzPanelClose` closes the panel from inside." />

    <section>
        <h2 data-toc class="scroll-mt-20">Resizing</h2>
        <p>Set <code>Resizable</code> to add a drag handle on the edge that faces the content. The size is clamped between <code>MinSize</code> and <code>MaxSize</code>, which accept any CSS length, and a bare number means px. The drag runs in the browser, so it tracks the pointer without an interop call per move.</p>
        <p>When the drag ends, the size in px arrives in <code>SizeChanged</code>. Persist it and pass it back through <code>Size</code> to restore it on the next visit.</p>
        <p>The handle sits centered on the panel's edge and takes the same options as the <a href="docs/components/resizable">Resizable</a> component. <code>Handle</code> picks the affordance:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><code>None</code> is a bare strip with no visual feedback.</li>
            <li><code>Line</code> shows a thin centered line on hover and drag.</li>
            <li><code>Grip</code>, <code>Dots</code>, <code>Knob</code> and <code>Pill</code> add a grip on top of that line.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><code>RevealOnHover</code> hides the grip until the handle is hovered, focused or dragged, and <code>HandleContent</code> replaces it with your own. <code>HandleClass</code> restyles the strip, while <code>Cursor</code> and <code>DragCursor</code> replace the OS resize arrows.</p>
    </section>

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Default"
          Description="Opening and closing animate the panel's width between 0 and `Size`, which defaults to `20rem`, while its siblings move aside. The counter button outside keeps working while the panel is open, because nothing is trapped or covered."
          Example="typeof(PanelDefaultExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Sides"
          Description="`Side` docks the panel to any edge. `Start` and `End` are logical edges that flip in right-to-left layouts, while `Top` and `Bottom` push content vertically inside a `flex-col` parent."
          Example="typeof(PanelSidesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Floating"
          Description="`Variant` decides whether the panel reads as part of the content or as its own surface. `Attached`, the default, sits flat with one shared border, while `Floating` insets it from the edges as a rounded card with a border and shadow. Both work with every other option, resizing included."
          Example="typeof(PanelFloatingExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Tall scrolling content"
          Description="A page-level panel should stay in the viewport instead of stretching down to where long content ends. Pin it with `Class=&quot;sticky top-0 self-start h-svh&quot;` so the page scrolls past while the panel stays one screen tall and scrolls its own body. This demo stands in for the page with a scrollable box, so it uses `h-96`."
          Example="typeof(PanelScrollExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Resizable"
          Description="With `Resizable` set, the panel gets a drag handle on its content-facing edge, clamped between `MinSize` and `MaxSize`. This one uses the `Knob` grip and reveals it on hover."
          Example="typeof(PanelResizableExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization"
          Description="Every part accepts `Class`. Here `HandleClass` colors the handle's hover line with `after:` utilities, since the strip itself is the full-height hit area, and `HandleContent` swaps in a custom grip."
          Example="typeof(PanelCustomExample)" />

    <Demo Title="RTL"
          Description="Inside a right-to-left `DirectionProvider`, the default `End` panel docks to the left edge and the resize handle's drag direction flips with it."
          Example="typeof(PanelRtlExample)" />
</div>

@code {
    // The anatomy drawn by the Composition section - CompositionTree computes the connectors.
    private static readonly CompositionNode Anatomy = new("BzPanel",
        new CompositionNode("BzPanelHeader",
            new CompositionNode("BzPanelTitle"),
            new CompositionNode("BzPanelClose")),
        new CompositionNode("BzPanelContent"),
        new CompositionNode("BzPanelFooter"));
}
